  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The hereby approved demolition must be completed within 5 years beginning from the date of this consent.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed demolition shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the documents submitted (Site Specific Demolition Method Statement, Ecological Appraisal (Ref: 6473 EcoAp vf /JD/KK/RL/DW/TS, Prepared by Aspect Ecology), Site Location Plan (ref. C-353-TP-01), Site Notice, Demolition Notice, Arboricultural Impact Assessment (ref: 11381_AIA.001 Rev A, Prepared by: Aspect Arboriculture), Phase I/II Contamination Assessment, Cover Letter- Received 10/03/2023; Outline Construction Logistics Plan (Version 1.3, Prepared by Mode Transport Planning), Construction Environmental Management Plan (Version A, Prepared by Chancerygate) - Received 06/04/2023) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 3 - No development shall take place until a finalised Construction Logistics Plan (CLP), written in accordance with current TfL guidance, has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The CLP shall include: \r\n(a)\ta site plan (showing the elements set out below);\r\n(b)\tconfirmation that a pre-start record of site conditions on the adjoining public highway will be undertaken with Hounslow Highways and a commitment to repair any damage caused;\r\n(c)\tprovision for the parking of vehicles of site operatives and visitors;\r\n(d)\tprovisions for loading, unloading and storage of plant and materials within the site;\r\n(e)\tdetails of access to the site, including means to control and manage access and egress of vehicles to and from the site for the duration of demolition;\r\n(f)\tdetails of vehicle routeing from the site to the wider strategic road network;\r\n(g)\tthe erection and maintenance of security hoarding;\r\n(h)\tprovision of wheel washing facilities at the site exit and a commitment to sweep adjacent roads when required and at the request of the Council;\r\n(i)\ta scheme for recycling/disposing of waste resulting from demolition; \r\n(j)\tmeasures to ensure the safety of all users of the public highway especially cyclists and pedestrians in the vicinity of the site and especially at the access;\r\n(k)\tcommitment to liaise with other contractors in the vicinity of the site to maximise the potential for consolidation and to minimise traffic impacts;\r\n(l)\tthe use of operators that are members of TfL's Freight Operator Recognition Scheme (FORS) and are FORS Silver accredited or better.\r\nThe approved CLP shall be adhered to throughout the demolition period\r\n"
  ],
